language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Job shop: each job visits its tasks in the listed order, each machine runs one task at a time, finish every job as early as possible.
given n_tasks : int(1..)
given jobof, machineof, dur : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_tasks)] of int(1..)
letting horizon = sum(dur)
find start : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_tasks)] of int(0..horizon)
find makespan : int(0..horizon)
branching on [start]
minimising makespan
such that
$ every task ends by the makespan
forAll a : int(1..n_tasks) . start[a] + dur[a] <= makespan,
$ within a job, a task starts after the task listed before it has finished
forAll a : int(1..n_tasks-1) . (jobof[a] = jobof[a+1]) -> (start[a] + dur[a] <= start[a+1]),
$ two tasks on the same machine never overlap: one of them ends before the other starts
forAll a, b : int(1..n_tasks) . (a < b /\ machineof[a] = machineof[b]) -> ((start[a] + dur[a] <= start[b]) \/ (start[b] + dur[b] <= start[a]))
